    },
    {
      "_id": "1kPXVToInZey741R",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!KioeAEZP78U0Coz5.1kPXVToInZey741R",
      "name": "Storyteller Notes",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p><strong>Layout:</strong> reception, open-plan desks (the analysts), a conference room with a corkboard covered in photos (Helen&#39;s podcast included), a locked armory, and a white room with high-intensity UV lamps, an “interview room.”</p>\n<p><strong>Occupants:</strong> Dana Okafor (@UUID[JournalEntry.bJA2iRyDgbm2TcuK]{Dana Okafor}), S. Hale (@UUID[JournalEntry.D611Mcr17F6HHEUw]{Sasha Hale}), and the tactical team @UUID[Actor.abaWg7NwNQvM0sDc]{FIRSTLIGHT Tactical Team}, which spends its nights in a warehouse at the port, not here.</p>\n<p><strong>Danger:</strong> breaking in here is the fastest way to raise the Thermometer (+3 if the intrusion is discovered: <button type=\"button\" class=\"sbn-termometro\" data-sbn-termometro=\"+3\" data-motivo=\"Intrusion discovered at Northline\"><span class=\"sbn-termometro-cambio\">+3</span> <span class=\"sbn-termometro-motivo\">Intrusion discovered at Northline</span></button>). Watching the place is more useful than going in.</p>\n<p>It doesn&#39;t appear in any set scene. Save it for the chronicle or for a very bold coterie.</p>\n"
      },
